  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Executor API (/executor/v1/)",
      "items": [
        "garden: GET status (agents_wanted), PUT agents",
        "gmail-triggers and watchlist (request_routes): GET requests (claims them), POST results, PUT agents, POST heartbeat",
        "Every call needs Bearer GARDEN_EXECUTOR_TOKEN and is refused with an Origin or a Cloudflare tunnel header; the tunnel never routes the prefix",
        "The list from letta agents list goes to each sidecar that answered, once per run, when any of them asks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Not a boundary",
      "items": [
        "Agents are root in the app-server and can read the token: they can read, claim or forge what the executor sees",
        "So both sides validate the other's data; garden shows names as escaped text and links only ids shaped like agent ids"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Install and isolation",
      "items": [
        "lettucectl up installs run.mjs, the token and the cron file only with garden-gmail-triggers, garden-watchlist or garden-code-server on; the vault alone gives it no work",
        "The token lives in the container layer, not under state/, so up reinstalls it after every recreate",
        "garden keeps the agent list in memory: no volume, default network only, no connection to Lettuce"
      ]
    }
  ]
